 gates are mainly performed in solution, and the obtained results are collective averages, making in situ observation of the computational process of individual DNA logic gates and accurate evaluation of their computational performance challenging. Here, a directional strand polymerization-based approach for constructing logic gates on DNA origami is developed. DNA switches assembled on the surface of DNA origami serve as monomers in a hybridization chain reaction after activation by input strands, enabling directional transmission of DNA signals, thereby executing defined logic functions. By assembling a reporter to terminate strand polymerization, the results of DNA logic operations can be recorded in situ through single-molecule fluorescence signals. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) A DNA-based system for selecting and displaying the combined result of two input variables (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/286374565_A_DNA-based_system_for_selecting_and_displaying_the_combined_result_of_two_input_variables)\nciteturn36search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Show abstract ... The Strategy of Constructing DNA Logic Circuits Based on DNA Origami Substrate ... The operations of the logic circuits are completed on the DNA wire track through the proximal hairpin circuit cascade. ... ‘Bottom-up fabrication’, which exploits the intrinsic properties of atoms and molecules to direct their self-organization, is widely used to make relatively simple nanostructures.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDynamically NAND gate system on DNA origami template - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0010482519301349)\nciteturn36search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; ## Abstract ... Zhang and coworkers used a series of DNAzyme-based logic gates to control DNA tile self-assemb